{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/y90nupkv","slideIndex":0,"text":"This slide compares the architectures, inputs, and outputs of the three models. Function fitting uses a smoothing spline to estimate the distance between the fingertips from the current normalized distance l_t. The MLP takes five distance values from the last five frames and produces one output through two hidden layers of 32 units each. Starting at movement onset, the LSTM reads one distance value at a time, carries a 32-dimensional hidden state forward, and estimates the fingertip distance at each time step. All three models output the estimated fingertip distance d̂_t at the current time step, in millimeters."}